    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\dfrac{x}{2}+1$",
      "worked": "When $x=0$, $y=1$, so $c=1$. For each increase of $2$ in $x$, $y$ increases by $1$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}m&=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}\\\\m&=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\y&=\\frac{x}{2}+1\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
